A||||9||JSocha||Anybody else getting tired of the media hyping the tragedy by using kids?||||8||
Z||000000||JSocha||09-27-2001||02:51 PM||||Although we all witnessed an American tragedy two weeks ago which is a very hard thing to recover from emotionally, I'm slowly getting tired of the media using children's emotions to hype up the event.<P>Yesterday and lastnight on the news I witnessed the "interviewer" literally leading the kids they were interviewing into the answers they and the public wanted to hear.  <P>Made my wife and I very ill to watch.  <P>Many of the kids seemed more like they wanted to go out and play then talk about it.  Some didn't even really know what happened.<P>Playing on the feelings and emotions of children who some don't even know what they need to feel.<P>When my wife and I discussed it lastnight while we were watching and we both came to the same thought that in most cases, this does not effect the child as much as it would an adult, because we look at the world and events much differently and how it effects us daily then what a child does.<P>Yes it may be important that they know what happened.<BR>Yes it may be important to explain what is happening.<P>But NO! It is not appropriate to tell a child how to feel when giving an interview.<P>"You are upset because this happened, aren't you?"; "This makes you and your friends angry deep inside and has hurt your family, right?"; "You will remember this and never forget about what these terrible people did?"; etc....I'm sure you have witnessed this your self.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Now on top of it, Reverand Jessie Jackson is considering on visiting the Taliban/Afghanastan while Bush is asking him not to go as it may relay a false sense of "negotiations", all because the little Rev. got an invitation and he is thinking on going.  <P>If he does go, I really hope that some terrorist over in Afghanastan puts a cap in his behind.  Fine...he has helped in similar situations and succeeded with a good outcome.  <P>However, this is one area I think and feel he should definately stay out of and let President Bush do what needs to be done to stop terrorism.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||09-27-2001||03:45 PM||||Yeah, every time I hear about something "for the children", it makes me want to gag and retch.<P>Damn, are adults not human, too?<P><BR>EDIT - typo <p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
